{:edb/db-before-t 634 :edb/db-after-t 635 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533947 50 #inst "2026-10-05T16:13:01.442Z" 13194139533947 true] [17592186087661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267881 13194139533947 true] [17592186087661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267888 13194139533947 true] [17592186087661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267919 13194139533947 true] [17592186087661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267942 13194139533947 true] [17592186087661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267977 13194139533947 true] [17592186087662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267860 13194139533947 true] [17592186087662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267867 13194139533947 true] [17592186087662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267874 13194139533947 true] [17592186087662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267914 13194139533947 true] [17592186087665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267898 13194139533947 true] [17592186087665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267924 13194139533947 true] [17592186087665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267956 13194139533947 true] [17592186087665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267963 13194139533947 true] [17592186087666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267905 13194139533947 true] [17592186087666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267931 13194139533947 true] [17592186087666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267936 13194139533947 true] [17592186087666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267949 13194139533947 true] [17592186087666 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267970 13194139533947 true] [17592186087985 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533947 true] [17592186087985 1145 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}\\ge 0$, there is no $y$ such that $\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=-\\frac{5}{4}.$ Therefore, the ellipse has no $y$-intercepts, meaning that it does not intercept the $y$-axis at any point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/assets/e2d4eadef6206fee8006028477c30337e2019000c33ed971f1f048294ef72615.png)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186088398 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533947 true] [17592186088398 1145 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{4}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{2}{3} & =1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+2 & =3 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =-5,\\,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(-3,0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/assets/f491b886477531fbd081cbdd73244e9cf489bd2474528ea27b66b187b9eb170e.png)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267861 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1089 "q-16642" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1100 "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1113 #uuid "fca3c3f7-188d-5506-9818-be66c0607803" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267860 1145 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{20}{9}} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(3-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267862 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267863 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267864 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267865 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267866 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1041 "selection" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267864 13194139533947 true] [17592186267861 1110 #uuid "06d0653b-a7e0-51d3-b91c-7d5c19f29317" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267862 1034 "There is no $x$-intercept" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533947 true] [17592186267862 1111 #uuid "dcf660b4-d4f5-5e3c-bbc1-0920eaadb2d9" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267863 1034 "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3},0)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533947 true] [17592186267863 1111 #uuid "7538da33-4499-5a56-8ee1-78740b96168b" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267864 1034 "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533947 true] [17592186267864 1111 #uuid "f715465a-681c-5546-aaf4-b72dcccc54c4" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267865 1034 "(-3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533947 true] [17592186267865 1111 #uuid "ef1a01ae-c095-5d05-8219-c89f6c6f83db" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267866 1034 "(\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},0)" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533947 true] [17592186267866 1111 #uuid "8d804631-6000-5274-9589-897a4691f407" 13194139533947 true] [17592186267867 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267868 13194139533947 true] [17592186267867 1089 "q